notes.front:
**updateTodo(todo, changes)**

Write `updateTodo(todo, changes)`: return a new todo with `changes` applied. `changes` may contain any subset of a todo's fields — and nothing else.

```ts
interface Todo {
  title: string;
  done: boolean;
  priority: number;
}

function updateTodo(todo: Todo, changes: Todo): Todo {
  return todo;
}
```

notes.back:
// Why: Partial<Todo> is Todo with every property optional, which is exactly what a patch
// is.
// Docs: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/utility-types.html
interface Todo {
  title: string;
  done: boolean;
  priority: number;
}

function updateTodo(todo: Todo, changes: Partial<Todo>): Todo {
  return { ...todo, ...changes };
}

